{%- comment -%}
  templates/page.our-story.liquid — Brand Story

  Assign this template to a page in Shopify admin:
    Online Store → Pages → Our Story → Theme template → "our-story"

  The page's own body content, if any, renders in the Heritage section, so
  the copy stays editable in admin. The literals below are fallbacks that
  make the page presentable before anyone writes anything.

  Timeline markers are a semantic <ol> — this is a sequence, and a screen
  reader should hear it as one.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="story-page">

  {%- comment -%} ============ HERO ============ {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="story-hero">
    <div class="story-hero__inner container">
      <p class="pv-eyebrow">Est. in the temple towns of Tamil Nadu</p>
      <h1 class="story-hero__title">
        Jewellery that remembers<br><em>where it came from</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="story-hero__lede">
        Every Paavai piece begins the same way it did generations ago — with a sheet of
        hallmarked gold, a steel stylus, and an artisan who learned the craft from the
        person sitting beside them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <span class="story-hero__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ============ HERITAGE ============ {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="story-section container" aria-labelledby="StoryHeritage">
    <div class="story-section__grid">
      <div class="story-section__body">
        <p class="pv-eyebrow">Our heritage</p>
        <h2 id="StoryHeritage" class="story-section__title">A craft passed hand to hand</h2>

        {%- if page.content != blank -%}
          <div class="rte">{{ page.content }}</div>
        {%- else -%}
          <p>
            Paavai grew out of a workshop where nakshi work, temple motifs and jadau setting
            were never treated as heritage techniques to be preserved — just the way things
            were done. The Lakshmi on a haram, the peacock on a choker, the uncut diamond
            held in a bed of gold foil: each of these carries a vocabulary that predates the
            brand by centuries.
          </p>
          <p>
            We work with goldsmiths who still finish by hand. A single temple haram can take
            a month, because the nakshi detailing on the reverse — the side no one sees —
            gets the same attention as the front. That is not romanticism. It is how a piece
            survives being worn by a granddaughter.
          </p>
          <p>
            What we have changed is everything around the craft: transparent gold rates,
            honest making charges, certification you can verify, and the ability to see a
            piece on your own neck before you commit to it.
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <figure class="story-section__media">
        {%- if page.metafields.custom.story_image -%}
          <img src="{{ page.metafields.custom.story_image | image_url: width: 900 }}"
               alt="{{ page.metafields.custom.story_image.alt | default: 'A Paavai artisan at work' | escape }}"
               loading="lazy" width="450" height="560">
        {%- else -%}
          {%- render 'paavai-placeholder', title: 'Our workshop' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ============ TIMELINE MARKERS ============ {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="story-timeline" aria-labelledby="StoryTimeline">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="story-timeline__head">
        <p class="pv-eyebrow">How a piece is made</p>
        <h2 id="StoryTimeline" class="story-section__title">From ore to heirloom</h2>
      </header>

      <ol class="story-timeline__list">
        <li class="story-marker">
          <span class="story-marker__dot" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'paavai-icon', icon: 'award', size: 22 -%}
          </span>
          <h3 class="story-marker__title">Heritage Craftsmanship</h3>
          <p class="story-marker__text">
            Nakshi, temple and jadau techniques worked by goldsmiths who trained under
            the previous generation. Motifs drawn from the same iconography that fills
            the gopurams a few streets away.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="story-marker">
          <span class="story-marker__dot" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'paavai-icon', icon: 'hammer', size: 22 -%}
          </span>
          <h3 class="story-marker__title">Handcrafted Precision</h3>
          <p class="story-marker__text">
            Every stone is set by hand, one at a time. Gemstones are ethically sourced
            and traceable to their supplier, and each diamond piece leaves with its
            gemological documentation in the box.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li class="story-marker">
          <span class="story-marker__dot" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'paavai-icon', icon: 'shield', size: 22 -%}
          </span>
          <h3 class="story-marker__title">Modern Design Standards</h3>
          <p class="story-marker__text">
            BIS hallmarking on every gold piece, published making charges, and a
            lifetime exchange. Traditional form, contemporary accountability.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ============ CLOSING CTA ============ {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="story-cta">
    <div class="container story-cta__inner">
      <h2 class="story-cta__title">Come and see the work</h2>
      <p class="story-cta__text">
        Book a consultation at the flagship, or have a piece brought to you on video.
        No obligation, and no pressure to buy on the day.
      </p>
      <div class="story-cta__actions">
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="btn btn--gold">Book a consultation</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="btn btn--outline-light">Browse the collection</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
